# ModelLogue Environment Variables

# --- Docker Compose ---
TIMEZONE=Asia/Tokyo

# --- Frontend (Vite) ---
# SR-139: the SPA calls its backend services under same-origin relative
# prefixes by default (/plantuml, /n8n, /nswitch). Leave these UNSET for
# the production stack (the reverse proxy maps the prefixes to the
# containers) and for local `npm run dev` / `npm run preview` (the Vite
# proxy in vite.config.ts maps them to the Docker Compose services). This
# keeps the built bundle free of absolute URLs, so the same image deploys
# to any host without a rebuild.
#
# Only set these to override with an absolute cross-origin URL (e.g. a
# remote service in a bespoke setup):
# VITE_PLANTUML_SERVER_URL=
# VITE_N8N_BASE_URL=
# VITE_NSWITCH_BASE_URL=

# Slack relay (SR-132–135): disabled unless set. For the same-origin
# stack, point it at the n8n prefix:
# VITE_SLACK_RELAY_BASE_URL=/n8n

# Debug: route AI chat through a local mock instead of n8n (dev only).
# VITE_USE_MOCK_AI=false

# --- n8n ---
# Gemini API key is configured inside n8n UI (Credentials), NOT as an
# environment variable. This keeps secrets out of files and follows the
# "no secrets in code" principle.
